Create a workflow, use sequence or flow chart: 
Open amazon application and search for books from 2026 in Amazon search bar

Assignment: Amazon Search Automation
Objective
Create a UiPath workflow using a Sequence or Flowchart to open Amazon and search for "Books from 2026" using the Amazon search bar.

Workflow Type Used
Sequence
A Sequence is suitable because the automation follows a simple step-by-step process.

Activities Used
Sequence
Use Application/Browser
Type Into
Click
Delay

Steps
Step 1: Create a New Project
Open UiPath Studio.
Create a new Process project.
Open Main.xaml.
Step 2: Add a Sequence
Add a Sequence to the Designer Panel.
The Sequence will contain all the automation activities.
Step 3: Open Amazon
Add the Use Application/Browser activity.
Indicate the Amazon website in the browser.
Enter:
https://www.amazon.in/
This opens Amazon in the selected browser.

Step 4: Enter Search Text
Inside Use Application/Browser, add a Type Into activity.
Indicate the Amazon search bar.
Enter:
Books from 2026
The Type Into activity enters the search text into the Amazon search bar.

Step 5: Click the Search Button
Add a Click activity.
Indicate the search button/magnifying-glass icon on Amazon.
This performs the search.

Step 6: Add a Delay
Add a Delay activity after the Click activity.
Set the delay to a few seconds.
This gives Amazon time to load the search results.

Workflow Structure
Sequence
   ↓
Use Application/Browser
   ↓
Type Into
"Books from 2026"
   ↓
Click
Search Button
   ↓
Delay
   ↓
Search Results Displayed

Activities and Their Purpose
Activity	Purpose
Sequence	Provides the linear workflow structure
Use Application/Browser	Opens and interacts with Amazon
Type Into	Enters "Books from 2026" into the search bar
Click	Clicks the Amazon search button
Delay	Allows time for the search results to load

Result
The workflow opens Amazon.in, enters "Books from 2026" into the Amazon search bar, clicks the search button, and displays the corresponding search results.
